WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.169 --> 00:00:05.910
Hello everyone, and welcome to this introductory class on Twinmotion.

2
00:00:06.309 --> 00:00:09.470
My name is Amea Yassine and I will be your guide today.

3
00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:15.070
Today we'll look at Twinmotion, a real-time visualization tool based on Unreal Engine.

4
00:00:15.859 --> 00:00:21.960
Twinmotion was originally developed as an architect's tool, but has developed since to cater for other markets.

5
00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:27.730
You'll experiment with a typical workflow, first by ingesting data into Twinmotion.

6
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:34.159
You then learn to add context and embellish the scene with the help of an extensive assets library.

7
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:43.579
This enables you to add materials, characters and vehicles among other things, using a very easy and intuitive workflow.

8
00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:50.700
You'll also learn to create and store your own user library, which you can then use across other projects.

9
00:00:51.679 --> 00:00:55.679
You'll learn to create and scatter vegetation for a more natural environment.

10
00:00:56.590 --> 00:01:02.689
Once you have finished this course, you may opt for a follow-up class that teaches you other tools in Twinmotion.

11
00:01:03.479 --> 00:01:07.480
These include creating and adjusting man-made lights for night scenes,

12
00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:13.480
as well as outputting media to disk in the form of images, panoramas and videos.

13
00:01:14.099 --> 00:01:18.040
But first things first, let's start with the basics.
